tem, and any questions) Tj T* (about it should be raised with the local Quality Assurance representative.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Section 4 - Cleanroom Environment. Grade B cleanrooms are maintained at a temperature of) Tj T* (18 to 22 degrees Celsius and a relative humidity of 30 to 60 percent. Environmental) Tj T* (monitoring results outside these limits must be escalated to the production supervisor) Tj T* (immediately. This section applies to all HelixNova Pharma manufacturing and packaging) Tj T* (sites and to contractors working on their behalf. The document owner reviews this section) Tj T* (every two years as part of the periodic review of the quality management system, and any) Tj T* (questions about it should be raised with the local Quality Assurance representative.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Section 5 - Change Control. All changes to validated equipment, processes or computerized) Tj T* (systems require a formal change request. Change requests are approved by the Change) Tj T* (Control Board, which is chaired by the Head of Quality Assurance. This section applies to) Tj T* (all HelixNova Pharma manufacturing and packaging sites and to contractors working on their) Tj T* (behalf. The document owner reviews this section every two years as part of the periodic) Tj T* (review of the quality management system, and any questions about it should be raised with) Tj T* (the local Quality Assurance representative.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Section 6 - Annual Product Quality Review. An annual product quality review \(APQR\) is) Tj T* (prepared for every commercial product. The APQR must be completed and approved by 31 March) Tj T* ET
